    field max_frohun_p type="i32::str" {
        key "SziK4Xg1"
        doc "setMaxfrohunP @0x131A884 (paired with this key in the DefineMst readParam @0x13D58D4).  The HUNTER ORB CAP -- 3 in this data.  ChallengeHeaderInfo::getAubeMax @0x125819C is a straight forward to it, and decFightRestTimer stops regenerating once the count reaches it.  Note this is the cap the CLIENT clamps to, which is why an earlier probe sending 4/5/6 read back as 3/3/3 and could not tell the three Aube fields apart."
    }

    field max_achieve_point_unit_per_day type="i32::str" {
        key "j1zaSBm7"
        doc """
        setMaxAchievePointUnitPerDay -- the Merit POINTS a player may earn in one
        day from trading UNITS.

        RENAMED from `unk16` 2026-09-15, which carried "TODO / not used in last
        version".  It is used: `deliverDailyCap` had no unit column to read, so
        units fell back to the ITEM ceiling and the Trade Units screen quoted
        the wrong field.  Both are 99999 in this data, so nothing was ever
        mis-enforced.

        Recovered from DefineMstResponse::readParam with tools/readparam_map.py.
        Adding it as a NEW field rather than renaming this one is what broke the
        build: two fields on one key makes Glaze fail to build its key hash
        (`static assertion failed: bool(hash_info<T>.type)`), which is what that
        error means.

        NOTE the two halves of the client's "Trade Limit x/y" do not agree: y is
        this POINTS cap, x is the deliver subject's progress, which counts
        UNITS.  Settling that wants a capture from the live game.
        """
    }

