json DefineEnergyRecover {
    doc "A one-field DefineMst block (response key VkoZ5t3K) carrying just the header energy-refill threshold.  DefineMstResponse::readParam @0x13D5068 never resets the singleton — each key has its own strcmp and setter — so this updates the threshold and leaves every other define as Initialize set it.  Sent by UserInfo, HomeInfo and MissionEnd so the threshold follows the player's level."

    field action_point_threshold type="i32::str" {
        key "eRQvzLeF"
        doc "The player's own max energy (UserLevelMst energy for their level): the header then says ENERGY_RECOVER_GEM_MAX_THRESHOLD exactly when energy is at or above max, and offers the refill below it."
    }
}

json FunctionReleaseMst {
    doc """
    F_FUNCTION_RELEASE_MST — WHICH FEATURE EACH `function_id` IS, AND WHAT
    UNLOCKS IT.  12 rows, function ids 8-19, read 2026-09-20 out of the
    client's own cached `Ver10_FA69am2p.dat` (encode key `tLaGZ8h3`).

    ★ ROW 9 IS THE SUMMONER AVATAR ARC: its condition is `2:10864`, and 10864
    is "The Holy Emperor" — the Karna Masta fight in Menon that the wiki names
    as what opens the arc.  That is what finally pinned the arc's gate down.

    NO WIRE KEY, like FrontierGateRewardMst: the client loads this from its own
    MST store and the binary defines no FunctionReleaseMstResponse, so the
    wrapper `F_FUNCTION_RELEASE_MST` is server-side only.  The server cannot
    change these conditions -- it can only EVALUATE them and report the result
    through `UserReleaseInfo` (Dp0MjKAf) on UserInfoResp, which is the only
    lever it has over feature locks.

    Ids 1-7 never appear here; those are the client's hardcoded early gates.
    """
    hash "F_FUNCTION_RELEASE_MST"

    field function_id type="i32::str" {
        key "JHYubaBP"
        doc "The client function this row gates.  Joins to UserReleaseInfo.function_id."
    }

    field param type="str" {
        key "t5R47iwj"
        doc "Empty on all 12 shipped rows.  // UNVERIFIED: no consumer read."
        optional #true
    }

    field condition type="str" {
        key "eyOHR7lB"
        doc """
        `type:param`.  **type 2 = the mission named by param has been cleared**
        (eleven of the twelve rows).  Type 4 appears once, as "4:4", on row 8
        and is not decoded.  An unrecognised type must be treated as NOT
        released rather than as released, or a feature opens for free.
        """
    }
}
